// The set piece library (plan §7.2) and the signature stacks (§7.4). A piece's kind is the code that realises it; its
// numbers are here. cost is terrain budget units (§3.3): a climb or descent costs cost + costScale x (g / g_main) x
// (length / 4 km); a tunnel cost per 300 m, +1 on a grade, +1 curved; a weak trestle +costScale. crunch: a piece
// the sawtooth builds up to (§7.1). minD / fullD: the difficulty it's allowed from, and where it reaches its full
// form. weight: how often it's picked among what fits, before the biome's bias (biomes.json "pieces").
// hardBend (ARCHITECTURE §8 note 278): a bend that derails the train under its top speed, laid only by the tier's
// count (tiers.json "bends"), so weight 0; its radius comes from the tier's bendDerail. Straight track either side
// (tangentM, halved where room is short), the hill it goes round on the inside (spurM high) and a fall on the outside
// (fallM). Not a crunch: like brass it's a demand, kept a braking distance from the next by the lethal spacing check.
// An S-bend (note 359, tiers.json "sBends"): two turns of sDeflectionDeg either way at the same radius, sGapM of straight
// between, held as one (the first turn's limit runs on till the train's tail is round the second): one demand over both.
{
  "pieces": [
    { "id": "straight", "kind": "straight", "minD": 0, "fullD": 0, "lengthM": [200, 2500], "cost": 0, "costScale": 0, "crunch": false,
